Flare for Ubuntu 24.04

The flare-inference package installs /usr/bin/flare. Run `flare --help` for
commands, `flare run --help` for serving, and `flare orbit --help` for cluster
management. Model packages are downloaded separately. Serving requires a
compatible NVIDIA driver; the DGX OS driver provides the CUDA driver library.

To register a host agent, run `flare agent install` as the user who will run
models. It prints a pairing code and installs a systemd user service. Installing
or upgrading this Debian package does not start or restart any service.

The agent installer keeps its own executable under ~/.local/lib/flare-agent.
After upgrading this package, run `/usr/bin/flare agent install` during a
maintenance window to update and restart that user's agent. Existing controller
identities and model caches are retained. Run `command -v flare` to check whether
another executable in ~/.local/bin or /usr/local/bin takes precedence.

Ignition, model weights, the CUDA toolkit, and Python are not included.

To share prefix checkpoints, use --prefix-cache-pool HOST:PORT for plain TCP
on a trusted fabric, tls:HOST:PORT for TLS, or unix:PATH for a local socket.
TLS verifies the manager against the host CA bundle, or the file given by
--prefix-cache-pool-ca (accepted only with tls:). The manager enables TLS only
with --tls-cert and --tls-key. Client and manager network modes must match.
